; pcrec VM program listing (DD-8; docs/design/engine_m4.md S10)
;
; Produced BY the emitter's own walk, not by a second walk over the
; AST: every line below was written by the same call that wrote the
; corresponding C. S10's one constraint -- "the dump must be derived
; from the same structure the emitter walks, never a parallel
; description" -- is therefore structural here, not a discipline.
;
; pattern      (?:a|ab){2,3}+
; engine       vm (forced by: possessive quantifier at pattern offset 13)
; prefilter    NO (--engine=vm) -- the VM scans from search_from itself (R21 E-6)
; rungs        frames-bounded -- see the RUNGS section below for which quantifier took which
; strategies   possessive -- see the STRATEGIES section below for which quantifier took which
; possessify   0 of 1 source quantifier possessified (eng_brep_design.md S2)
; caps         RX_NCAPS 1 (0 capturing groups in the pattern text)
; step budget  500000000 backtrack resumptions
; capacities   3 resume frames, 2 trail entries (exact: no subject ceiling)
; program      22 labels, 68 events
; resume pts   4
; max replicas 3 (limit 64, checked before emission)

SLOTS (the slot_values array, engine_m4.md S2.4)
  slot         holds                  note
   0,1         $0 whole match         written by the ENTRY, not the VM (S3.4)
  (no empty-iteration guard slots: no nullable unbounded quantifier on the frames rung)
  (no span-loop low-water slots: no cursor rung in this program)
  2            cut mark               resume-stack depth at entry -- a possessified loop's (eng_brep_design.md S2) or an atomic group's ([M6.4.2])

RUNGS (engine_m4.md S2.5; D46's per-quantifier stamp)
  at L0      frames-bounded     frames rung, bounded {2,3}, greedy, ATOMIC (a written cut: one frame for the whole loop, no giveback)

STRATEGIES (eng_brep_design.md S2; D47.3's per-quantifier stamp)
  at L0      possessive     frames rung, bounded {2,3}, greedy, ATOMIC (a written cut: one frame for the whole loop, no giveback)

PRUNING (k23_design.md; D51's per-quantifier stamp)
  ceiling: the subject end -- either no prefilter, or the prefilter's window END is not a bound on this match's end: the pattern carries an ATOMIC GROUP (atomic_groups_design.md 4.4 H3) or a LOOKAROUND (lookaround_design.md 5.6), or the prefilter was built from the COUNT-COLLAPSED superset (prefilter_count_independence.md 2 H3, K39/[OPT-4]) -- the `; prefilter` line above says which
  bound sites emitted: 3
  runtime-term length retreats: 0
  at L0      clamped      frames rung, bounded {2,3}, greedy, ATOMIC (a written cut: one frame for the whole loop, no giveback)

PROGRAM
  L0      ; possessified repeat: record the resume-stack depth to cut back to
         set     slot_values[2] <- scan_position ; possessive cut mark (resume-stack depth at loop entry)
         -> L2
  L2      ; MRL: mandatory copies left plus the follow do not fit
         ; MRL: mandatory copies left plus the follow do not fit
         -> L4
  L4      ; alternation entry (2 branches)
         PUSH    resume L7                    ; branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
         -> L5
  L7      ; alternation resume: try branch 2 of 2
         -> L6
  L5
         consume 'a'                          -> L3
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L6
         consume 'a'                          -> L8
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L8
         consume 'b'                          -> L3
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L3      ; MRL: mandatory copies left plus the follow do not fit
         ; MRL: mandatory copies left plus the follow do not fit
         -> L10
  L10     ; alternation entry (2 branches)
         PUSH    resume L13                   ; branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
         -> L11
  L13     ; alternation resume: try branch 2 of 2
         -> L12
  L11
         consume 'a'                          -> L9
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L12
         consume 'a'                          -> L14
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L14
         consume 'b'                          -> L9
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L9      ; possessified optional copy (1 remaining)
         ; work charge: frames discarded by this cut
         CUT     frames <- slot_values[2]     ; cut: the previous copy is committed, its choice points are dead
         ; MRL: no room for another copy and the follow
         PUSH    resume L15                   ; the loop's ONLY frame: this copy failing leaves the loop
         -> L16
  L16     ; alternation entry (2 branches)
         PUSH    resume L20                   ; branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
         -> L18
  L20     ; alternation resume: try branch 2 of 2
         -> L19
  L18
         consume 'a'                          -> L17
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L19
         consume 'a'                          -> L21
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L21
         consume 'b'                          -> L17
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L17     ; possessified repeat: every copy taken
         ; work charge: frames discarded by this cut
         CUT     frames <- slot_values[2]     ; cut: the loop is complete and owns no live choice point
         -> L1
  L15     ; possessified repeat: a copy could not run -- exit with the iterations that did
         -> L1
  L1      ; the pattern is complete
         -> accept
  accept   ; return scan_position - ctx->pos; the capture slots at this instant ARE the answer (S3.1)
  fail     ; the ONLY backtracker and the only indirect jump; one step charged here (S4.2)

CHOICE POINTS (preference order: the frame pushed at a site resumes the LESS preferred alternative)
  at L4      resume L7      branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
  at L10     resume L13     branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
  at L9      resume L15     the loop's ONLY frame: this copy failing leaves the loop
  at L16     resume L20     branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2

DFA ISLANDS (0)
  (none: no flat alternation in this program has a finite literal language, so src/gen/emit_vm.c's alternation island declined every one -- docs/spec/tuning.md S2.20)

CALLOUT SITES (0)
  (none: module 'callouts' has no producer, so no pattern can reach a call site -- engine_m4.md S9.1)
